      "message": "Yes... but...\n\n`btm_scn` is defined like this: `uint8_t btm_scn[BTM_MAX_SCN_];`\nand `BTM_MAX_SCN_` is coming from \n`#define BTM_MAX_SCN_ 31  // PORT_MAX_RFC_PORTS packages/modules/Bluetooth/system/stack/include/rfcdefs.h`\nand finally `#define PORT_MAX_RFC_PORTS 31`\n\n\nIf the return value is now \"from 2 to PORT_MAX_RFC_PORTS - 1 included\", that mean that the max scn returned is `PORT_MAX_RFC_PORTS - 1`, and that mean the highest value of `scn_idx` is `PORT_MAX_RFC_PORTS - 2` so the last index of the array is not used.",
